halo infinite season 2 details are here  as well as an explanation for the forge  delay  343 industries has shared new details on  halo infinite season 2 lone wolves which  launches on may 3rd for arena  multiplayer 343 is adding a new map  catalyst which will be available on  multiple playlists at launch the king of  the hill and attrition modes will be  added to new playlists while the motion  tracker better known as radar will see  improvements to its outer edge detection  for big team battle the new map breaker  will be available on season 2 launch day  and in a very exciting development  multiplayer announcer jeff steitzer's  voice will be added for medals that  players earn big team battle also gets a  fix in the season 2 update for a bug  that caused weapon racks to spawn  asymmetrically 343 also announced that  it's implementing a change to csr so  that the progress bar now reflects  results from the most recent match and  not the entire season melee combat  should be improved too as 343 says  players will be less likely to phase or  whiff on beat down chances thanks to  network improvements additionally melee  damage is being decreased by 10 percent  on all weapons for the mangler  specifically players will need to hit  two shots and a beat down to earn a kill  additionally the ravager's base shot now  sees a damage buff for equipment the  drop wall gets a slight performance  increase while the overshield becomes  more powerful as well providing slightly  more shielding in terms of vehicle  changes collision damage aka splatter  for the chopper will be increased the  banshee's agility and damage output  meanwhile will be increased to help  players dominate better and finally the  warthog and razorback won't flip or  bounce as much with the season 2 update  you can see a full rundown of halo  infinite season 2 update highlights over  on gamespot.com and in other halo news  infinite's long-awaited forge mode which  lets players create all manners of  custom content missed the game's launch  last year and is likely still many  months away from release developer 343  industries has now explained the delay a  little more saying it was necessary to  ensure it reached 343's benchmark for  quality in a blog post the dev said  quote it broke our hearts to not be able  to launch forge alongside the rest of  infinite but to ensure it meets the bar  that we're setting for it to achieve  this massive overhaul to forge in  infinite just wasn't able to make it out  before the end of last year the new  version of forge will feature quote  another generational leap forward in  terms of its capabilities and the dev  added it will contain many of the  community's highly requested features  the mode is coming sometime during halo  infinite season 3 so it's still a long  time away from release members of halo  insiders will get to try it first and  provide input to 343 and according to  343 it will quote be worth the wait for  the forge community and fans of the  content they will be able to create and  before we close out 31 years after the  secret of monkey island and monkey  island 2 were getting returned to monkey  island this year the game's director ron  gilbert said on twitter that he's been  working on return to monkey island in  secret for the past two years the game  is being developed by terrible toybox in  partnership with lucasfilm games and  devolver digital and even though it's  slated for release this year there's no  word yet on a specific date or platforms  unfortunately i don't have an ounce of  nostalgia for the monkey island series  but let me know in the comments if  you're really excited so i can be  excited for you and also let me know  what you think about all of the new halo  improvements coming in may  i'll see you tomorrow
 

